12. FIRST THREE SECONDS (link-opened, cold cache)
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
t = 0 ms      HTML arrives. Inline critical CSS paints --bg plus an SVG board
              silhouette at 12% opacity. theme-color already applied, so the
              iOS status bar and Android nav bar are the game's colour.
t = 0 ms      Synchronously parse ?g= from location.search and render
              "Joining Sarah's game..." into #status. The player knows the
              link worked before a byte of WebGL has loaded.
t <= 100 ms   First Contentful Paint. Never a white flash, never a bare spinner.
t 100-1500ms  Module chunk + GLB stream in. Determinate 3px progress bar driven
              by THREE.LoadingManager.onProgress (loaded/total). If total is
              unknown, switch to an indeterminate shimmer — never freeze at 0%.
t <= 2500 ms  First rendered frame. Camera performs a 600 ms ease-out settle
              from polar 0.28 -> 0.62 rad. That motion IS the affordance: it
              tells the player the scene is 3D and draggable, no tutorial needed.
t 2500-4000   One ghosted hand glyph + "Drag to look. Tap a tile." fades out on
              the first successful orbit OR after 4 s, whichever comes first.
              No modal. No carousel. No dismiss button.

