Reduced motion:
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
const RM = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
const prefersReducedMotion = () => RM.matches;
const DUR = () => RM.matches
  ? { intro: 0,   cameraFit: 0,   pieceMove: 120, dice: 0,   capture: 100 }
  : { intro: 600, cameraFit: 250, pieceMove: 320, dice: 900, capture: 380 };
RM.addEventListener('change', invalidate);
With reduce set: no intro camera settle, no idle camera drift, no particle
burst on capture, dice resolve by a 200 ms cross-fade straight to the face.

